Body:
I think you might need to explicitly set the custom manager key to `azure`, as only then does it register the azure model loader which has 

```json5
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "azure": {
      "name": "U-M GPT",
	  "whitelist": ["gpt-4o"], // hide other models available from the azure loader
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/azure",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.umgpt.umich.edu/azure-openai-api/openai",
        "apiVersion": "2025-04-01-preview",  
        "apiKey": "{env:API_KEY}",
        "useDeploymentBasedUrls": true,
		"useCompletionUrls": true,  // only available in the azure handler
        "headers": {
          "openai-organization": "{env:SHORTCODE}",
        },
      },
      "models": {
        "gpt-4o": {
          "id": "gpt-4o",
          "limit": {
            "context": 128000,
            "output": 16384
          }
        },
      },
    }
  }
}
```

I'm not sure about your `apiVersion`. It seems that these are the stable versions Rest API specs: https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/tree/main/specification/cognitiveservices/data-plane/AzureOpenAI/authoring/stable.

You might still need to set the environment variable `AZURE_API_KEY`. Because there is currently a bug that if it is not set, the azure loader is skipped and `useCompletionUrls` has no effect. Or you should leave out `apiKey` from the config and run `/connect` inside opencode to configure the custom azure provider.
